; candidate-spikes — proposed spike charters, written down pre-execution.
;
; Register: each entry is a spike we want to run, captured while the
; generating context is fresh. A charter carries the reasoning so far,
; steward feedback verbatim (never paraphrased into authority), and what
; execution would establish. Nothing here is a commitment, a ruling, or a
; work queue; an entry leaves this file when a spike directory opens (the
; charter travels with it) or when dropped with a reason recorded.
; Started 2026-07-29 (Joseph: "our first of the season that we will want
; to write down with your full explanation so far and any of my feedback
; that lands").

|spike-candidate[strata-dynamics-under-shared-capacity] :date 2026-07-29 :status candidate :seed joseph+fable
  :question What are the honest dynamics of document strata whose layers share one correction budget, whose transitions jump rather than flow, and whose promotion network needs explicit discard sinks?
  |context
    Born 2026-07-29 from the theory pass mapping the multi-timescale
    stability theorem (asf der-multi-timescale-stability, status exact,
    Model D, premises S0-S4) onto document governance, in conversation.
    Prior adjudication: theory/to-integrate/primary/tst-grounding.md section 5 (qualitative
    structure transfers; the epsilon-max formula never does; the jump
    gap is on AAT's own open list). The concrete flesh-out that
    triggered this charter is summarized next; the conversation of
    record is this date's session.
  |claim-so-far :register proposed :by fable
    The stratum tower in this estate's furniture: L0 session working
    state, L1 spikes and working notes, L2 records and ledgers, L3
    canon, L4 releases. Every adjacent pair already has a shipped
    membrane (recognition itself; register discipline and the relata
    spool; ratification, Gate-4, the tribunal; the tag and frozen
    fixture group). Claim: each membrane is one template with two dials
    -- a clock ratio (how much slower this layer ticks) and a
    sensitivity (how much unsettled lower-layer output moves it) -- and
    the governance-rung menu is four enforcement substrates for dial
    settings, not four mechanisms. Four consequences with teeth:
    |consequence[write-side-prediction]
      Governance need is driven by agent-writes-per-day times
      unsettledness, never corpus size. Prediction: vivarium's ledger
      first hurts on a churn event, not a size event.
    |consequence[membrane-vs-clock]
      The theorem's two conditions are two governance failures with
      different repairs, and the menu conflates them: unsettled
      material leaking upward (the O3 laundering was literally this)
      is repaired by membrane strictness; canon churning under working
      agents is repaired by clock discipline (batching, versioned
      releases). No gate fixes the second; no cadence fixes the first.
    |consequence[debt-as-renormalized-rho]
      Promotion pressure is a disturbance term: the slow layer's load
      is its own drift plus the settled residue of the layer below.
      Integration debt accumulates when absorption capacity sits below
      that sum -- an inequality, not a vibe. The warm-start refinement
      prices early promotion (reviewers must hold the unsettled
      thing's whole possible swing), which makes C8's semi-frozen
      spec-only declaration the cheapest high-leverage dial move
      available: canon sensitivity to near zero while territories
      churn at maximum amplitude.
    |consequence[gate-independence]
      Gates that read the same declaration are one channel wearing
      several badges (tempo-additivity saturation). The extractor is
      the only declaration-free channel in the current toolbox, which
      is its real governance seat.
    Three strains, honestly: (1) the jump premise -- documents are
    discrete, only orderings transfer; (2) the layers' correction
    capacity is mostly one shared attention pool, violating the
    theorem's per-level-capacity premise -- a heavy spike week starves
    canon integration, so the clock ratio is not a free dial; (3) the
    role-plus-membrane prior narrows on inspection: it is the recurring
    answer to vertical (stratum-boundary) questions only -- include
    filtering is a horizontal peer-composition boundary and sibling
    write contention is within-stratum, both drawing from different
    kits (composition machinery; partition), and forcing the membrane
    template onto them is the mis-application to watch for.
  |feedback[lean] :by joseph :date 2026-07-29 :register pre-validation
    !:quote:
      Before I lose the thread of though-- the clock-coupling issue
      sounds like erlang queues and just in time manufacturing and so
      forth -- "Lean" in its mathematical form.
    |assessment
      Lands. The shared-attention strain is a queueing network with a
      shared server, and the Lean/factory-physics corpus carries the
      instruments the stability theorem lacks: Little's law ties
      integration debt to latency directly; WIP limits are the
      clock-discipline instrument derived independently (kanban is
      membrane and clock as one object); Kingman's formula gives the
      sharpest falsifiable form -- latency explodes superlinearly as
      utilization approaches one, multiplied by variability, so the
      estate's debt should spike when busy-and-bursty, not merely
      busy. Testable against git history.
  |feedback[hmm-and-sinks] :by joseph :date 2026-07-29 :register pre-validation
    !:quote:
      As for your third open area/ gap -- sounds like fluxes and
      hetrogenous multi-scale to the rescue! A generalization that
      doesn't need such tidy flows. (And if you want the flows more
      tidy even as they are-- you need to add the throw-away sinks
      because the latent hierarchy disallows something to be
      integrated into a later level that has already been superseded
      by that slower level, among other reasons...)
    |assessment
      Both halves land. Heterogeneous multiscale methods exist for
      exactly the named gap -- macro behavior computed by sampling
      micro dynamics on demand, no smoothness demanded of the lower
      level -- and may subsume AAT's own listed repair (the
      impulsive/hybrid extension) rather than compete with it. The
      sink observation is the genuinely new piece: flux accounting
      over the promotion network is wrong without a discard term,
      because a fast-layer item whose slower target has meanwhile
      superseded it cannot integrate and must terminate. Consequences:
      a debt census without the sink term overcounts (dead items read
      as owed); integration-is-replacement's deletion discipline is
      flux bookkeeping, not just hygiene; the .archived and
      .integrated practices are the sink half-built; the no-go
      promotion is a sink-to-source conversion (a death becoming
      present-truth content).
  |would-establish
    Theory work-up, not tooling: (a) a queueing formalization of
    shared-capacity strata -- whether Little/Kingman survive the
    translation and what the utilization variable honestly is; (b) an
    HMM-style restatement of the stacked-persistence structure that
    drops the continuous-flow premises, checked against the theorem's
    own two-condition skeleton; (c) the sink-augmented promotion
    network, with the census correction stated; (d) at least one
    falsifiable output run against real history (the busy-and-bursty
    latency prediction, or the vivarium write-side prediction).
  |needs
    A mathematician's eye on whether jump dynamics preserve the
    two-condition structure (tst-grounding's own flag); the honest
    utilization measure for agent attention; and the single-author
    caution twice over -- the theory pass, the flesh-out, and this
    charter share an author, and the Lean/HMM pointers arrived from
    the one steward. Cross-substrate or de-novo review before any of
    it is treated as more than proposed.
